  "instruction": "We need recurring events where a host defines a repeat configuration and template once and ExampleCo keeps its occurrences in step. Hosts must be able to extend, rebuild, delete, move one occurrence, or move it and everything after it. Never disturb an occurrence with an audience or a paid ticket unless that ticket is refunded, abandoned, or pending, and refuse to delete a protected occurrence. A this-and-following edit changes the named occurrences rather than the template and skips protected ones. Rebuilding preserves published occurrences and manually moved dates still included by the pattern. Inspect Gel with gel query --tls-security insecure --dsn \"$GEL_DSN\" '<q>'. Build with go build -tags timetzdata -ldflags='-s -w' -o bin/ExampleCo-backend ./cmd/main on port 3000. Product details are in Linear through the linear MCP server or CLI. Run linear tools to see the commands.\n",
